noncomputable section ProofPart_HalfSpaceDerivativeHolder


/- The flat boundary derivative caller. A genuine H1 extension with
zero value on the opposite half-space supplies the Dirichlet trace.
The derivative, original equation and extension are identified through
actual Sobolev value fields. This yields a Holder bound for every
continuous classical representative of that derivative's gradient on
the positive side, arbitrarily close to the face. -/
open Set Metric Filter MeasureTheory TopologicalSpace TauCeti TauCeti.PDE InnerProductSpace
open scoped NNReal InnerProductSpace Distributions Gradient
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
namespace ConformalPoisson
variable {n : ℕ}
local notation "V" => EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))

without_proof_info in
theorem holderOnWith_unit_directional_forcing {f : V → ℝ} {K α : ℝ≥0} {S : Set V}
    (hf : HolderOnWith K α f S) (e : V) (he : ‖e‖ = 1) :
    HolderOnWith K α (fun x => (-f x) • e) S := by
